---

## Project Description

This project is a simple command-line line editor developed in C.

A line editor is a basic text editor that works with one line at a time.
Instead of moving freely around a document like a modern text editor, the
user interacts with the document using commands and line numbers.

The editor allows the user to create, view, and modify a small text document
directly from the terminal.

The project demonstrates the use of C programming concepts such as data
structures, functions, strings, arrays/dynamic memory, and command-line
input handling.

---

## Implemented Features

### 1. Insert a Line

Adds a new line of text at a specified line number.

**Usage:**

```text
insert <line_number> <text>
